  "raw": {
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Faculty-Secretary_JR-1214-1": {
      "title": "Faculty Secretary",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-09-03\nPosted: Posted 5 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Faculty Secretary Full- or Part-Time: Full time Exempt or Non-Exempt: No Hourly Rate: 21.10 USD Hourly Department: College of Education (PM) Job Description: JOB SUMMARY: To perform secretarial/clerical duties and serve as a liaison for faculty members, including adjunct faculty and departmental professional and technical staff. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Perform secretarial duties: may include answering telephones, provide information or route calls to appropriate person; prepare, type, proof and otherwise assist with materials prepared by faculty members; create basic event flyers; duplicate printed materials; prepare and send faxes and E-mail; maintain files; greet visitors and students, ascertain nature of business, and direct them to the appropriate person, department, etc. Perform clerical duties: may include ordering paper and office supplies; deliver packages; distribute information; schedule service for office equipment; provide copy machine assistance; maintain key and fax log; complete billing meter reading, etc. Maintain faculty advising and lead faculty list for departments. Attend department meetings and take minutes. Process, maintain, and manipulate data on a personal computer. Serve as a liaison with students, other staff, and visitors when a faculty member is away from the office. Maintain confidentiality of exams, tests and department personnel files and records. Assist faculty with communication /letters to students, host teachers and school principals. Complete travel expense requisitions. Order and coordinate the requisition of course texts for faculty and adjunct faculty classes. Assist faculty with obtaining non-confidential student information for programmatic updates, evaluation, and planning (i.e., identify students' remaining courses for a degree program for faculty course planning). Assist with the coordination of COE events. Provide clerical support on course scheduling documents. Update wall displays. Take meeting notes, type agenda, creating calender invitations and reminder emails. Maintain distribution log for gift card reimbursement. Track items that require approval. Track and maintain inventory. Retrieve course evaluations each semester and deliver any paper course evaluations. Provide backup assistance for co-workers when necessary or requested. Proctor make-up and other special circumstance exams for students. Update and post faculty office hours and class schedules. Perform other duties as requested or required. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Work direction is provided as determined by the assignment or project; functional supervision is received from the assigned faculty Coordinator; and administrative supervision is received from the assigned Dean. SUPERVISION EXERCISED: May be responsible for the coordination of work for student employees, including selection, training and evaluation. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: High school diploma or equivalent. Two years of job-related experience. Strong oral, written, telephone, and interpersonal communication skills. Excellent spelling, grammar, punctuation, and basic mathematic skills. Ability to work cooperatively and communicate professionally with faculty, staff, students, and the general public. Experience and ability to positively interact with all members of the campus community. Ability to organize and prioritize daily activities and expedite workload under occasional time pressure. Ability to work independently or as a member of a team, with minimum supervision, and accept direction from multiple and diverse faculty members. Ability to occasionally handle differing, non-routine work situations based on standard procedures and policies. Ability to maintain confidentiality of files and records. Ability to learn technical/discipline-specific terminology. Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodation. WORKING CONDITIONS: Duties are generally performed on-campus, inside and not exposed to adverse conditions. The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job, and shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job. It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision. The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. For eight consecutive years, SVSU has been recognized as a “Great College to Work For” (2016-2023). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2023). SVSU fields 19 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,   http://www.svsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/International-Early-Childhood-Education-Fellow_JR-1256": {
      "title": "International Early Childhood Education Fellow",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-25\nPosted: Posted 14 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title: International Early Childhood Education Fellow Full or Part Time: Part time Hours: 29 Exempt: Yes Supervisory Org: International Fellow (JM-AJ) Job Description: JOB SUMMARY:    Responsible for providing workshops on early childhood education at SVSU partner schools in the People’s Republic of China. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBLITIES INCLUDE: Travel to the People’s Republic of China to live and teach workshops on early childhood education for periods of 4 to 8 weeks in Spring semester (March, April, May, and/or June) or in Fall semester (end of August, September, October, November, and/or December). Teach SVSU curriculum in classrooms of approximately 50 students for 12 to 24 hours per week. Participate in training on how to teach SVSU approved curriculum on early childhood education. Provide appropriate grading and assessment to classes. Provide administrative support, as required, for the Office of International office. Provide training support for other Fellows teaching classes or preparing to teach classes at Changchun Normal University. Serve as an ambassador from SVSU to students, faculty, and staff at Changchun Normal University. Perform other duties as assigned SUPERVISION RECEIVED:    General supervision is received from the Dean of the College of Education. SUPERVISION EXERCISED:   This position will not supervise any other positions. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Master’s degree in Early Childhood Education or related field Must be able to independently live and work in China for periods ranging from 4 to 8 weeks during scheduled workshops Must be able to write and speak English fluently Must be able to work very well with people of diverse ethnic and socioeconomic backgrounds Experience and ability to positively interact with all members of the campus community Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodations. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Travel and/or lived aboard experience Experience teaching early childhood education or working in an early childhood education setting BENEFITS: International Flight from DTW to Changchun, China Housing All meals on CCNU Campus Cell phone Global Data plan for use while in China WORKING ENVIRONMENT & EMPLOYMENT CONDITIONS: Duties are generally performed inside but include outside seasonal activities. All work associated with this role must be performed within the state of Michigan and China. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and throughout their employment. The university does not provide employment visa sponsorship now or in the future for this job classification.  Since SVSU does not participate in E-Verify, candidates for employment are not eligible for STEM OPT extensions. The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job. It shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty.   About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU was recognized as a “Great College to Work For” for 9 consecutive years (2016-2024). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2025). SVSU fields 20 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,  http://www.svsu.edu ."
