    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Custodial-Specialist_JR-1144-1": {
      "title": "Custodial Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-20\nPosted: Posted 19 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Custodial Specialist Full- or Part-Time: Full time Exempt or Non-Exempt: No Hourly Rate: 16.20 USD Hourly Department: Campus Facilities - 3rd Shift Custodial (PM) Job Description: Pay Range: $16.90 - $20.10 Scheduled Days: Sunday - Thursday 11 pm - 7 am JOB SUMMARY:   To perform various cleaning, set-up, and tear-down tasks within assigned areas; may include swimming pool, restrooms, locker rooms, hallways, multi-purpose arena, offices, classrooms, special purpose rooms, conference rooms, recital hall, theater; football stadium and its box office, press box, restrooms, concessions and fixed sitting areas. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Clean assigned areas following established schedules and prescribed methods; may include removing trash, sweeping and/or dust mopping floors, polishing hard surfaces, vacuuming carpets, cleaning windows and mirrors, dusting furniture, equipment, and ledges, wet mopping floors, vacuuming swimming pool, and washing off tabletops, countertops, equipment, and chalkboards. Arrange and set-up furniture, staging, athletic, and/or physical education activity equipment, etc. working from diagrams, written, and/or oral instructions. Tear-down and rearrange rooms/areas following the completion of activities. Lock and unlock building and rooms, close windows, and turn off lights. Sweep and/or remove debris, leaves, snow and ice from steps and walks at building entrances. Perform special projects as assigned; may include shampooing carpets, stripping and waxing floors, washing walls, windows, baseboards, scrubbing multi-purpose arena, weight room floors, and pool deck. Maintain assigned equipment for safety and cleanliness and report malfunctioning equipment. Load, unload, and move supplies. RELATED DUTIES: Observe and report the need for repairs and replacement of equipment, furniture, and fixtures. Move furniture and equipment as needed for cleaning purposes. Assist other custodial specialist and custodial personnel as required. Other duties as assigned. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Assignments and administrative supervision are received from the Associate Vice President and/or his designee(s). ​ SUPERVISION EXERCISED: May be responsible for student employees assigned to them. ​ MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: High School diploma or equivalent may be considered. Valid Michigan Driver License. One year of custodial experience. Ability to effectively communicate with others and maintain good working relations with supervisors, co-workers, and the University community. Ability to work alone or as member of a team, perform job duties within scheduled time limits, and adapt to flexible and emergency scheduling. Ability to apply and follow custodial specialist safety procedures. Knowledge of the proper use and care of cleaning equipment and solutions/chemicals. Ability to follow clearly defined oral and/or written instructions. Ability to perform the essential functions of the position with or without accommodation. Ability to pass any State/Federal mandated training, licensing, and/or certification requirements, within a reasonable period of time. Must pass job-related physical examination and relevant skill test prior to being appointed to the position. Ability to begin and follow through with the task(s) or plan identified in the job description, and to take the first step in performance of those duties and responsibilities.   Reporting of facilities or grounds maintenance needs which are observed. WORKING CONDITIONS: Most duties are subject to indoor environmental conditions, some duties may be performed outdoors for relatively short periods of time. Exposure to dust and cleaning chemical fumes.  Subject to noise and vibrations caused by automatic cleaning equipment. ​ The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job, and shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. For eight consecutive years, SVSU has been recognized as a “Great College to Work For” (2016-2023). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2023). SVSU fields 19 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,   http://www.svsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Administrative-Assistant-to-the-Vice-President-of-Governmental-and-Community-Affairs_JR-1243": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant to the Vice President of Governmental and Community Affairs",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-18\nPosted: Posted 21 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Administrative Assistant to the Vice President of Governmental and Community Affairs Full or Part Time: Full time Hours: 32 Exempt: Yes Supervisory Org: Governmental and Community Affairs (PM) Job Description: JOB SUMMARY:  Provides administrative and operational support to the Vice President of Governmental and Community Affairs. Manages executive-office workflow, Governmental Affairs administration, operations of the SVSU Community Development Fund, financial and records systems, and day-to-day direction of student employees. This full-time position reports to the Vice President of Governmental and Community Affairs. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Manage and prioritize the Vice President's calendar, meetings, travel, briefing needs, correspondence, and follow-up to priorities of the Office of Governmental and Community Affairs. Assist with Governmental Affairs administrative workflow, including official and legislative meetings, coordination with governmental-relations firms in Lansing and Washington, D.C. Prepare briefing folders, invitations, RSVP tracking, contact lists, issue and approved communications. Manage the administrative and financial operations of the SVSU Community Development Fund in conjunction with the Assistant Director of Community Affairs. Prepare, format, proofread, and retain routine correspondence and approved letters issued by the Vice President in conjunction with the Assistant Director of Community Affairs. Process Workday transactions, purchasing, invoices, deposits, PCard reconciliation for the Vice President. Assist with budget tracking, and reports; maintain records, files, shared calendars and inboxes, templates, and approved digital communications for the Office of Governmental and Community Affairs. Assist the Assistant Director of Community Affairs with various after hours programming around the Great Lakes Bay Region. Engage with various special projects for the Office of Governmental and Community Affairs. Provide day-to-day work direction for student employees, including scheduling, training, task assignment, and timesheet review. Exercise sound judgment, confidentiality, and tact with University leadership, public officials, and community partners. Work on campus, remotely when approved, and at off-campus locations; work occasional evenings and weekends and travel locally or regionally as required Perform other similar duties as assigned by the Vice President. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: General supervision is received from the Vice President of Governmental and Community Affairs. SUPERVISION EXERCISED : Provides day-to-day work direction, scheduling, training, and timesheet review for student employees. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Associate degree in a related field, or an equivalent combination of education and progressively responsible experience. Four years of progressively responsible administrative experience, including support for an executive or senior administrator. Experience with executive calendars, correspondence, meetings, governmental or committee workflow, purchasing, invoices, or expense processing, budgets, and records. Excellent written, oral, interpersonal, organizational, customer-service, confidentiality, and administrative-judgment skills. Proficiency with Microsoft 365 and ability to learn Workday, electronic communication, web-content, and other specialized systems. Ability to work independently, prioritize deadlines, interact effectively with all members of the campus community, work occasional evenings or weekends, and travel locally or regionally.  Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodations. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor's degree in a related field. Executive support experience in higher education, governmental affairs, public administration, or state / local government.   WORKING ENVIRONMENT & EMPLOYMENT CONDITIONS: Duties are performed in an office environment, remotely when approved, and at campus, governmental, community, and off-campus locations. Work involves frequent computer and telephone use, and occasional evening or weekend assignments. All work associated with this role must be performed within the state of Michigan.     Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and throughout their employment. The university does not provide employment visa sponsorship now or in the future for this job classification.  Since SVSU does not participate in E-Verify, candidates for employment are not eligible for STEM OPT extensions.   The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job. It shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU was recognized as a “Great College to Work For” for 9 consecutive years (2016-2024). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2025). SVSU fields 20 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,  http://www.svsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Clerical-Pool_JR-40-1": {
      "title": "Clerical Pool",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-17\nPosted: Posted 22 Days Ago\nPart time\n\nJob Title: Clerical Pool Full or Part Time: Part time Hours: 5 Exempt: No Supervisory Org: Clerical Pool (JM) Job Description: Job Summary:    Responsible for temporary clerical assignments on an as needed basis in various departments within the University.  To support administrative and secretarial staff with high level of office assistance.  Interact effectively with University  faculty, staff, and the public.  Responsibilities may include but are not limited to answering telephones, photocopying, filing, maintaining calendars, performing word processing, using other various computer programs, cashiering, and other duties as assigned. This is an on-call, as needed position and hours may vary. Minimum Qualifications :  High school diploma or GED.  Ability to effectively communicate verbally and in writing. Strong attention to detail. Preferred Qualifications:   Previous secretarial experience.  Experience with personal computers, Word, WordPerfect and Excel. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU was recognized as a “Great College to Work For” for 9 consecutive years (2016-2024). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2025). SVSU fields 20 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,  http://www.svsu.edu ."
