    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Senior-Transfer-Credit-Clerk_JR-1221-1": {
      "title": "Senior Transfer Credit Clerk",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Senior Transfer Credit Clerk Full- or Part-Time: Full time Exempt or Non-Exempt: No Hourly Rate: 19.20 USD Hourly Department: Registrar Support (PM) Job Description: JOB SUMMARY:  To assist the Associate Registrar in the implementation of the Registrar's component of the student transfer process; including working with the Michigan Transfer Agreement (MTA) and new relevant technology, maintain computerized transfer credit records for undergraduate and readmitted students, assist in the interpret of transfer course equivalencies, and process guest student applications. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Download and verify transfer transcripts, Advanced Placement test scores, CLEP test scores from appropriate sources and determine authenticity.  Ensure scanning and uploading of relevant documents into document management system. Monitor workflow(s) for transcript evaluations. Assist in determination of acceptability of transfer credits for undergraduate and readmitted students, based upon predetermined course equivalencies data.  Review transfer credits for credit duplications, grades, and MACRAO/MTA agreements. Obtain and review transfer credit authorization and distribute Transfer Evaluation Reports. Process and maintain guest student applications for SVSU students attending other institutions, verifying GPA/grades and eligibility to return to SVSU, and assist Associate Registrar in corresponding with students on how proposed courses transfer to SVSU. Maintain catalog updates from other institutions and make changes in SVSU’s Transfer Equivalency database Maintain the security and confidentiality of grades, GPA's and transcripts and other student records in accordance with FERPA regulation. Provide customer services at the front counter to students, parents, staff/faculty members, and the general public in the implementation of policies and procedures of the Registrar's Office. Provide clerical support for cleaning up/revising the existing transfer credit database. Provide clerical support with the implementation of any new State and University led transfer projects/pathways Assist with the transfer equivalency process. Provide clerical support for the revision and maintenance of the transfer website. Most of the work will include text entry and proofreading. Assist Associate Registrar with continual benchmarking of other Michigan institutions for competitive transfer practices and web communications. Assume the clerical duties to assist the Associate Registrar with the Transfer Credit Procedural Manual materials for department chairpersons and deans. Send letters after determining transfer credit will not be awarded, stating the reason for the decision. Enter transcript information for international students. Verify report at the end of every semester confirming that all transfer transcripts have been evaluated and are scanned in ImageNow; verify that Second Bachelor's degree student's waivers are entered when needed Answer phones and provide information regarding the ordering of transcripts, status of course petitions, verification of enrollment, dates of graduation, status of graduation applications/degree audits, readmit status, registration information, and route calls to the appropriate or SVSU staff member/administrator when necessary. Assist with student registration. Assist with  verification requests. Audit work output for accuracy and make necessary corrections. Perform other duties as assigned. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: ​ General supervision is received from the Associate Registrar.  Additional work assignments/direction and guidance may be provided by the Assistant Registrar and Registrar.   MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: High School diploma or equivalent. Two years of job-related experience, preferably in student records. Ability to work overtime hours as needed. Strong oral, written, telephone, and interpersonal communication skills. Excellent spelling, grammar, punctuation, and basic math skills. Demonstrated customer service orientated attitude. Proficient in Microsoft Office Suite (Word, Excel, PowerPoint, Outlook), and possess the ability to learn new or specialized software quickly. Ability to work cooperatively and communicate professionally with faculty, staff, students, and the general public. Experience and ability to positively interact with all members of the campus community. Ability to work independently or as a member of a team, with minimal supervision. Ability to organize and prioritize daily activities and expedite workload under occasional time pressure. Ability to handle differing, non-routine work situations based on standard procedures and policies. Ability to maintain confidentiality of files and records. Ability to learn technical/discipline specific terminology. Available for overtime hours when needed. Ability to regularly stand, walk, sit, balance, stoop, kneel, crouch, reach, handle, finger, talk, hear, see, and distinguish colors while performing the essential duties of this job. Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodation. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Additional education, training or certification in related area. Previous experience in higher education. WORKING CONDITIONS: Duties are performed on campus, inside, and not exposed to adverse conditions. Overtime hours may be required. The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job, and shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. For eight consecutive years, SVSU has been recognized as a “Great College to Work For” (2016-2023). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2023). SVSU fields 19 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,   http://www.svsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Coordinator-of-Alumni-Communication_JR-1240": {
      "title": "Coordinator of Alumni Communication",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-12\nPosted: Posted 27 Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Coordinator of Alumni Communication Full or Part Time: Full time Hours: 40 Exempt: Yes Supervisory Org: Alumni Relations (PM) Job Description: Salary Range: $48,000–$52,000 per year, depending on qualifications and experience . JOB SUMMARY:  The Coordinator of Alumni Communication supports the Executive Director of Alumni Relations by coordinating communications, digital content, and constituent data initiatives that advance the mission of the Alumni Relations Office, engage alumni and students, and enhance the University image. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Build, maintain, and manage Alumni Website to strengthen alumni engagement. Coordinate the Alumni Relation’s database and collaborate with other University offices with use of the CRM software. Coordinate data initiatives, database management, and on-going CRM maintenance. Execute writing, editing, production, and publication of all communications for the Alumni Relations Office. (Newsletters, mailings, email, social media, etc.) Create and maintain all communication tracks for individualized segments of the SVSU Alumni population. Assist with annual management and implementation of Commencement ceremonies. Assist with management and implementation of Alumni Relations events. Perform other duties as assigned. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: General supervision is received from the Executive Director of Alumni Relations. SUPERVISION EXERCISED : No formal supervision is exercised. The position may provide task guidance to student employees or temporary staff as assigned. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor's degree required.  Relevant experience in alumni relations, client development, student affairs, enrollment management, or customer service-related fields. Ability to think critically, plan strategically, and prioritize actions as they relate to the University's goals. Ability to perform multiple tasks. Excellent written, oral, and interpersonal communication skills. Strong computer literacy including word processing, spreadsheets, and database programs. Experience and ability to positively interact with all members of the campus community. Ability to utilize technical advances in alumni and development relations. Ability to work effectively with senior administrators, staff, and volunteers. Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodations. Willing to work evening and weekend hours when needed. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: Experience with Raiser’s Edge or a comparable advancement CRM, email marketing platforms, website content management, social media management, and communication development. WORKING ENVIRONMENT & EMPLOYMENT CONDITIONS: Duties are generally performed indoors, with occasional outdoor and seasonal activities. Some evening and weekend work and intermittent travel are required. All work associated with this role must be performed within the state of Michigan. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and throughout their employment. The university does not provide employment visa sponsorship now or in the future for this job classification.  Since SVSU does not participate in E-Verify, candidates for employment are not eligible for STEM OPT extensions. The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job, and shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU was recognized as a “Great College to Work For” for 9 consecutive years (2016-2024). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2025). SVSU fields 20 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,  http://www.svsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Career-Development-and-Technology-Specialist_JR-1220": {
      "title": "Career Development and Technology Specialist",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Career Development and Technology Specialist Full or Part Time: Full time Hours: 40 Exempt: Yes Supervisory Org: Career Services (PM) Job Description: JOB SUMMARY : The Career Development and Technology Specialist empowers students and alumni to achieve their career goals by providing individualized career advising, job search strategies, career readiness programming, and internship support. The position administers Career Services technology platforms, manages office data collection and reporting, supports employer engagement initiatives, and collaborates with campus and external partners to enhance career development opportunities. ESSENTIAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide career advising and support to students and alumni, including resume and cover letter reviews, mock interviews, and job search strategies. Administer and interpret the FOCUS2 Assessment to all students, identifying careers, jobs, and activities that closely align with their interests. Develop and deliver orientation, career readiness, and professional development programs and presentations for new and current students . Administer the university’s online career management platform, including approvals of external job postings and event requests. Manage and develop content for the Career Services website and social media platforms. Collect, analyze, and report data for the Career Services office, including administering the First Destination Survey; tracking office interactions, Co-op/Internship placements, and online database usage; and completing institutional reports for NACE. Coordinate marketing and communication efforts promoting Employer Partnership Program activities, career events, and employment opportunities to students in collaboration with the Employer Development Specialist. Coordinate opportunities to increase connectivity between faculty, students, alumni and external employer partners. Participate in the planning, coordination and implementation of various recruitment events. Assist with university retention initiatives and services. Other duties as assigned.   SUPERVISION RECEIVED: General supervision is received from the Director of Career Services  SUPERVISION EXERCISED:   None.  MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: Bachelor’s Degree. Three years progressively responsible experience in business, management, recruiting, career development, job placement, human resources or related work experience. Must have customer-service oriented attitude and demonstrable, successful customer-service experience. Strong interpersonal skills with an understanding of and enthusiasm for today’s undergraduate and graduate student experience. Excellent oral and written communication skills and networking skills. Experience and comfort with public speaking. Strong technology skills with proficiencies in Microsoft Office and the ability to learn specialized software programs. Experience with interpreting data and preparing reports. Strong planning and organizational skills - ability to manage multiple tasks. Ability to handle confidential and sensitive situations with diplomacy and excellent judgment. Experience and ability to work with all members of the campus community. Ability to attend occasional night and weekend events as needed. Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodation. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS: 1-2 years of experience within a postsecondary Career Services Office. Knowledge and use of career services software (e.g., Handshake). Professional experience in resume writing, interview coaching, career counseling, career coaching, life coaching or similar. Experience with PowerBI or Tabulu or other data reporting software. WORKING CONDITIONS: Duties are generally performed inside and not exposed to adverse conditions. Applicants must be legally authorized to work in the United States at the time of hire and throughout their employment. The university does not provide employment visa sponsorship now or in the future for this job classification.   The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job. It shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. SVSU was recognized as a “Great College to Work For” for 9 consecutive years (2016-2024). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.  SVSU is constructing the first university research facility on Lake Huron to improve public health and the economy in the Saginaw Bay watershed.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2025). SVSU fields 20 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,  http://www.svsu.edu ."
    },
    "https://svsu.wd503.myworkdayjobs.com/job/Main-Campus/Administrative-Secretary_JR-1200-1": {
      "title": "Administrative Secretary",
      "description": "Start date: 2026-08-04\nPosted: Posted 30+ Days Ago\nFull time\n\nJob Title: Administrative Secretary Full- or Part-Time: Full time Exempt or Non-Exempt: No Hourly Rate: 21.10 USD Hourly Department: Academic Advisement Center (PM) (Lisa Krissoff Boehm Job Description: JOB SUMMARY: Provide secretarial and administrative support to the Office of Academic Advisement and coordinate day-to-day office operations for the department. ESSENTIAL DUTIES & RESPONSIBILITIES: Provide secretarial support to the department, including: preparing reports and publications; scheduling appointments and meetings; answering telephones, providing information, greeting visitors, ascertaining the nature of the request, ; and making arrangements for appointments, meetings, facilities, and travel.  Coordinate all prospective student inquiries made by mail, phone, e-mail and in-person.  Work with Microsoft Teams, and Microsoft Bookings to set up and confirm appointments. Maintain data using word processing and database software; maintain and process computer information. Prepare, update and maintain student academic records for advising appointments. Provide departmental administrative support, including: assisting in the coordination of departmental projects and programs; assisting with the development and design of promotional campaigns and other materials. Perform basic clerical duties including opening and routing incoming mail, preparing outgoing mail, including bulk mailings; ordering supplies and monitoring email and faxes. Maintain and update curriculum guides and other resource materials. Maintain the security and confidentiality of grades, transcripts, and other student records in accordance with FERPA regulations. Responsible for generating monthly reports for the Academic Advisement Center. Assist the Director in monitoring student employment hours and process related forms and reports, such as timecards. Perform other duties as assigned. SUPERVISION RECEIVED: Supervision is received from the Director of the Academic Advisement Center or the designated departmental Administrative Professional.  Work assignment direction may also be provided by other departmental Administrative/Professional staff.   SUPERVISION EXERCISED: Assist with the supervision of student employees, including interviewing, selecting, training, scheduling and evaluating.     MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS: High School Diploma or equivalent, and additional education, training or certification in a related field.  Three years of job-related clerical experience, preferably in higher education, including excellent spelling, grammar, punctuation, basic math skills and oral and written communication skills. Demonstrated customer service skills and interpersonal skills to interface with faculty, staff, students, and the general public. Personal computer proficiency (Microsoft Office Suite) and ability to learn specialized software programs and Student Information Systems. Ability to work cooperatively and communicate professionally with faculty, staff, students, and the general public. Experience and ability to positively interact with all members of the campus community. Ability to work independently with minimal supervision and accept direction from multiple and diverse staff/faculty members. Ability to organize, prioritize, and expedite workload, working under occasional time pressure. Ability to occasionally handle differing, non-routine work situations and problems by exercising independent judgement and initiative. Ability to maintain confidentiality of files and records. Ability to learn technical/discipline-specific terminology. Ability to perform the essential duties of the position with or without accommodation. WORKING CONDITIONS: Duties are performed on campus, generally inside and not exposed to adverse conditions. The above reflects the general details considered necessary to describe the essential functions of the job, and shall not be construed as an exhaustive statement of duties, responsibilities, or requirements that may be inherent in the job.  It is not intended to limit or in any way modify the right of any supervisor to assign, direct, and control the work of employees under his/her supervision.  The use of a particular expression or illustration describing duties shall not be held to exclude other duties not mentioned that are of similar kind or level of difficulty. About SVSU: Saginaw Valley State University is a comprehensive university with more than 100 programs of study for its roughly 7,000 students. Located on a suburban campus in Michigan’s Great Lakes Bay Region, SVSU is committed to a supportive and empowering environment for students, faculty and staff. For eight consecutive years, SVSU has been recognized as a “Great College to Work For” (2016-2023). SVSU emphasizes undergraduate teaching and learning, and community-based research. SVSU earned the Community Engagement classification from the Carnegie Foundation for the Advancement of Teaching, a distinction achieved by only 7 percent of U.S. colleges and universities. By their senior year, 84 percent of students have engaged with community employers and agencies in internships, field placements or some other component of their academic preparation. SVSU is establishing itself as a leader in STEAM education for the Great Lakes Bay Region, partnering with businesses, foundations and school districts to improve students’ performance in math, science and the arts at the middle school, high school and university levels.   More than 70 percent of SVSU freshmen live on campus in student housing that has been rated No. 1 among public universities in the U.S. (2018-2023). SVSU fields 19 varsity sports at the NCAA Division II level. The average class size is 23 students. For more information, please visit our website ,   http://www.svsu.edu ."
